# Files where a change needs someone to say out loud why.
#
# The golden vectors are the contract's own statement of how the SDK must encode
# what it signs, and the API report is the record of everything the package
# publishes. A diff in either is either a deliberate decision or a bug, never
# noise, so neither should merge without one of us reading it.
#
# The rest are the code that decides what a user is asked to approve and what
# gets signed without one: the EIP-1193 provider and the error codes dapps
# branch on, the keys screens that render a request next to the call that signs
# it, and the CLI logic that lets a session key act with nobody watching.
#
# This file only auto-requests reviewers. It becomes a gate once `main` has a
# ruleset with "Require review from Code Owners", which the repo does not have
# today: the branch has neither classic protection nor a ruleset. Until then,
# treat the request as a convention.

